{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche","id":1486410,"title":"Multiple Fetiche","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-14T06:39:32-07:00","id":1486410,"title":"Multiple Fetiche","content":"From what i've read, you can only put 1 spirit in a tool/weapon/object to create a fetiche, but what about a composed tool?<br /> Let's take an exemple: you build an armor, you turn into fetiche each part of it (gloves, boots, helmet...) to create a single armor with multiple powers, let's say a wind spirit in boot to run faster, a war spirit in the helmet to increase accuracy with guns, steel spirits into the main part to increase it's resistance, and a fire spirit in the gloves to get additionnal fire damages to the punch.<br /> <br /> Would you allow that kind of thing and how would you manage to make it work? A single roll but with a certain amount of success to activate the entire armor (in that case 4 minimum), spend 4 gnosis point? Activate them 1 by 1?<br /> <br /> I've heard about the tattoo fetiche too, so a draw or a mark can be used to create a fetiche, then would you allows someone to add on a single tool multiple marks to give it multiple powers, and would you let it activate them all at once, or 1 by 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T07:17:28-07:00","id":1486413,"title":"","content":"I'm rather strict with fetishes, and as a house rule even count attuned fetishes to the total number of dedicated objects (ie permanent Gnosis limits the total number of dedicated objects <i>and</i> fetishes). One spirit per object, and composite objects (like your armor example) count as a single object. If the player wants to upgrade their fetish, they need to find a stronger spirit to bind into it. If they want multiple effects, they need to find a spirit that matches all these effects.<br /> <br /> I have multiple reasons for this, but mainly because I prefer characters to rely more on their innate powers, and because the mechanics get unwieldy after a certain number. If I had a player who wanted to focus on crafting fetishes as a character concept like this, I would probably cook up a house rule to pool the abilities of bound spirits and then activate them as needed for a fetish. I would still make them pay for each activation of a single power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T12:54:09-07:00","id":1486457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486413#post1486413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a player who wanted to focus on crafting fetishes as a character concept like this, I would probably cook up a house rule to pool the abilities of bound spirits and then activate them as needed for a fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why i ask, one of my pc want to specialise in craft, especially fetishes. His main goal is to build an armor with lots or special ability (shoulder cannon, bladed gloves, gravity boots...) all working with spirits. <br /> The goal is to create a new kind of praetorian guards for the Cairn, only the strongest garou will be allowed to use it and only in special occasion <br /> <br /> As the book doesn't talk about complex or multiple effect fetishes it's hard for me to house rule something: how many fetishes can be bound together? How would you use their powers? All at once for the passive effect? For how long?<br /> <br /> Too much details for me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T13:18:21-07:00","id":1486458,"title":"","content":"So:<br /> <br /> 1) A Fetish can house more than one spirit, though each additional spirit makes it increasingly difficult to do. Two is considered the height of spirit-craft, and three would be a legendary feat. Multiple spirits do not, generally, result in multiple powers, because the spirits have to be compatible with each other and work together towards a common purpose (that is, two spirit Fetishes are going to be stronger versions of single spirit Fetishes of a similar design.<br /> <br /> 2) Characters can use multiple Fetishes at once, and even split up something into smaller components to make each a Fetish. However doing so requires each to be activated separately.<br /> <br /> 3a) The spirits in Fetishes are sentient and sapient beings who do not appreciate being used as mere tools to grant powers. Spirits can refuse to be bound into a Fetish, and can rebel if they feel misused or taken for granted. Each Fetish a character is attuned to is also an NPC with needs they're responsible for seeing to, so the more they have, the more time they use up in their day keeping their Fetishes happy.<br /> <br /> 3b) The Garou Nation does not see Fetishes as private property. Mistreatment of the spirits via Fetish binding is grounds to have your Fetishes taken away from you by your fellow Garou because you're mistreating spirit allies, and punishment rites might get brought into the equation.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> So, basically? The intended controls here are meant to mostly be social. Imagine a character that invests in a dozen Retainers of varying dot values and specialties, and wants to constantly bring them around. Fetishes might address the logistical nightmare part of that, but not the social difficulty of managing all those NPCs as a cohesive unit. Fetishes can be complex in function, but no matter how many spirits you try to stuff in one, it's still going to have &quot;one&quot; power (even if mechanically it might have 2-3 related abilities) not one per spirit.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest reading Hammer &amp; Klaive if you haven't already. It doesn't completely address everything here, but it goes at lot farther than the core books do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T21:52:30-07:00","id":1486495,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, klaives are the only example of a fetish that has more than one spirit bound to them. One for the normal ability of a klaive to do aggravated damage, and the second for any special ability the klaive, or grand klaive, may have. It's one reason klaives are so difficult to make.<br /> <br /> So if you wanted to model anything, I would use that as my example.<br /> <br /> But I would personally limit how many spirits and powers are possible. I'd limit it to two. The first that allows the armor to soak, and the second for one extra power that makes sense for the armor.<br /> <br /> If I were the ST, I would not approve of things like an armor with a shoulder canon or gravity boots, and so on. That seems way too gonzo for how the setting and its fetishes are typically portrayed. And the time and chiminage needed to make one likely prevents a character from making multiple sets of them. WtA does not have the same assumptions about crafting like some versions of D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> If you want to make multiple fetishes that can be used together, you could do that. But each fetish would need to be activated separately. And of course, each fetish would need to be made separately and all the spirits separately negotiated with. Again, making even one fetish takes a long time and commitment. After he's created all these fetishes, he probably wants to do something else. Unless you intend your character to do nothing else for the next decade or more for making all of them.<br /> <br /> RPGs in general do not handle crafting well. The rules to do so are included to help the ST and PC create singular items important for the character. They are not meant as any kind of economic simulation, and the crafting rules don't reflect the true difficulty of creating all these items. Since as written, usually the crafting rules would imply far more fetishes, magic items, artifacts, or whatever than are actually present in the setting. As an ST, I'd have no problem with a PC devoting a portion of his time crafting one fetish, or over the course of an entire chronicle a few more. But if he intends to craft out a bunch for himself and then others, I wouldn't allow it. Crafting a fetish is essentially a spirit quest by itself. It's not something that should be shotgunned repeatedly. I'd start running the requirements to make a fetish a lot more severely, and requiring a lot more roleplay than just time and some dice rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T01:06:48-07:00","id":1486502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486457#post1486457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why i ask, one of my pc want to specialise in craft, especially fetishes. His main goal is to build an armor with lots or special ability (shoulder cannon, bladed gloves, gravity boots...) all working with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, this is something that would really be more fit for a Technocratic Convention rather than Garou. As the others pointed out, the culture of the Nation and the nature of Spirits makes Fetishes something really special. The Glasswalkers used to have a faction called Cyberdogs who specialized on techno-fetishes for body enhancements like this, and that didn't work out well for them.<br /> <br /> I can see the appeal of a weapon smith character as concept though. My advice would be to make the 'armor project' a long term thing for the player- if they fulfill their self-set goal after only a few sessions, it won't be very satisfying. Give them a Mentor smith who is on their way out and wants to continue their legacy with an apprentice, let them gather info on journeys to other Caerns, find rare materials they would need etc. Make the spirits of Fetishes characters that demand to be treated as individuals, with their own goals and personalities. As a journeyman, they could learn about all the points the others made in this thread and why crafting Fetishes is no trivial smithing.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, how about this:<br /> The armor set is a single fetish, as usual. Its function is that it can store and use 'charges' at will of the wearer. These charges are specifically crafted Talens for the armor, which produce the extra effects. For example, an 'air charge' would be Talen that temporarily increases speed.<br /> <br /> Talens are single use, so you can limit the total uses of the special armor effects with 'slots' and cap the power level. The spirits bound to them are usually also a lot less intelligent (although still sentient), so the creation as tools is less 'controversial'. More intelligent spirits of the same kind would still take offense if they aren't treated respectfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T01:16:36-07:00","id":1486504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486502#post1486502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanically, how about this:<br /> The armor set is a single fetish, as usual. Its function is that it can store and use 'charges' at will of the wearer. These charges are specifically crafted Talens for the armor, which produce the extra effects. For example, an 'air charge' would be Talen that temporarily increases speed.<br /> <br /> Talens are single use, so you can limit the total uses of the special armor effects with 'slots' and cap the power level. The spirits bound to them are usually also a lot less intelligent (although still sentient), so the creation as tools is less 'controversial'. More intelligent spirits of the same kind would still take offense if they aren't treated respectfully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea, I hadn't thought of that. I think my players will still want something more permanent than charges, but it's already a good basis for thinking.<br /> On the other hand it work well for the instant effect but what about some more passive, like additional Brawl or Firearms dots? Would you allows those kind of effect to last a scene or 1 turn? 1 Turn would fit the idea of charge but would take a lot of gnosis roll to activate each turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-15-2022, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T02:05:23-07:00","id":1486505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486504#post1486504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand it work well for the instant effect but what about some more passive, like additional Brawl or Firearms dots? Would you allows those kind of effect to last a scene or 1 turn? 1 Turn would fit the idea of charge but would take a lot of gnosis roll to activate each turn</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really up to you. As ST, you will need to balance the effects against whatever you plan to have the players fight with it. If you're unsure, run a few simulated battles outside of the sessions to see how it plays out.<br /> <br /> If you want to save on die rolls, you could give the Talens a flat effect (fixed damage, or fixed bonus) and instead of rolling Gnosis say the armor can activate a Talen if the wearer expends a Rage or Willpower point.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T10:02:20-07:00","id":1486533,"title":"","content":"Well i've already set that the effect of the fetishe/talen depend on the objet, a fire elemental in the armor can immune the wearer against fire, give him additional fire damage when he punch, melt something by contact... but if you put it in a shoulder cannon you can have a flamethrower or a plasma cannon.<br /> For those exemple the immunity to fire damage would last a scene while flamethrower would last 1 action<br /> <br /> If you would have to do it with fetishe instead of talen you would have to separate the different part of the armor<br /> The base full armor would have 1 effect, then the shoulder cannon would have another, the gauntlets blade could have another... as long as they're implemented on existing fetishe armor it would work<br /> <br /> It's balancing the idea inside the game which is hard, cause a smart pc could come with an idea allowing him to go with a big load of fetishes equipment, after fetishes aren't limited to wear by the gnosis of the garou in the rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T18:06:01-07:00","id":1486567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486533#post1486533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's balancing the idea inside the game which is hard, cause a smart pc could come with an idea allowing him to go with a big load of fetishes equipment, after fetishes aren't limited to wear by the gnosis of the garou in the rules</div> </div> </div> </div>It's limited by activation rolls, how many items you can attune to yourself and the fact that the spirits can totally not want to work together and feel they are belittled by someone carrying a dozen items treated as common equipment rather than sacred objects that need to be kept happy to actually keep working.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T06:09:41-07:00","id":1486611,"title":"","content":"You sure spirits can refuse to work in fetishes? Cause i remember reading that spirits are asleep when they're bond as talen or fetishes, in addition the Klaive description talk about klaive being used in simple challenge between 2 garou while the old garou complaining about their frequent usage for non vital purpose. <br /> If the spirits were still awake they would certainly rebelling against their wearer for these kind of usage, they were probably not being bond for this at the beggining","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T07:06:15-07:00","id":1486615,"title":"","content":"Yup. Spirits can refuse to work with anyone who shows them disrespect. They are not very active, but they are quite aware if the proper spiritual reverence is given or not given to them. And it's not like they can come out and complain, but they sure as hell can make your life miserable with the powers not working or silly things like your blade not cutting.<br /> <br /> That's of course if another Garou doesn't conclude you are abusing the spirits and messing up the ancient bargains, and proceeds to challenge you for them or just beat the ever living crap out of you and threaten to take them to a better home next time.<br /> <br /> Take care of your spirits, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 07-16-2022, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T11:31:50-07:00","id":1486645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486611#post1486611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You sure spirits can refuse to work in fetishes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Such fetishes are typically called cursed fetishes. It's up to the ST when this might be the case, as it's done pretty much for narrative purposes. The spirit is angry in some way and therefore the fetish is &quot;acting up.&quot; It might be because the spirit was forced into the fetish, the fetish is being maltreated in some way, the original agreement for binding the spirit to the fetish is violated in some way, or whatever else the ST thinks might justify for the spirit being angry. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> phrase that it is angry because it is not longer being treated as a &quot;sacred object&quot; seems the right take here.<br /> <br /> What are the affects if the spirit in the fetish is angry, making it cursed? Again, this is up to the ST. It might mean needing to spend more Gnosis, having a higher difficulty to activate, that it stops working entirely at times, that it subtracts to the dice pool instead of adding it, or some other very inconvenient response that makes the fetish very unreliable to use.<br /> <br /> Basically a cursed fetish is the spirit letting you know that it's best if you destroy the fetish and release the spirit because it isn't happy anymore for whatever reason. It's possible the spirit could be sufficiently appeased that it stops being cursed and the Garou can go back with using it with no concerns, but in many cases I would say many Garou would think it best to just release the spirit.<br /> <br /> Technically, the spirits in a fetish are in a kind of slumber, but it isn't identical to slumber as there have been many statements in multiple sourcebooks of the spirits in fetish being somewhat aware of its surroundings especially in regards of whether it is being properly treated. I imagine it's more like the spirit is shifting between a waking dream and light sleep, rather than the deep sleep that &quot;slumber&quot; usually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:06:13-07:00","id":1486680,"title":"","content":"Ok, but theorically a garou can wear as many fetishes as he can without limit except treating theme as sacred being, with honor and respect.<br /> <br /> So, still theorically, a pc can be stuffed only with fetishes, including tattoo and scar ones. And even in that case he would need to call them 1 by 1 by rolling or spendind gnosis. So far everything is working in the lore, but the rules does not say if you can spend more than 1 gnosis point or roll multiple times to activate fetishe, it doesn't even saying if it's a passive or active action, if it use you action in a turn like a punch or if it's like soak damages<br /> <br /> The ST will certainly define what is possible but still it's strange that the game talk about sacred object without talking about the possibility of characters fully stuffed with them, especially when no rule tell it's impossible. I know more than one pc that will try to play on this lack of detail","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:19:20-07:00","id":1486684,"title":"","content":"Again. Read Hammer and Klaive. You might be loaded with talens, you will never ever be loaded with fetishes. It's a commitment of time, resources and complete narrative detour to even pursue it, and anyone seen as a &quot;mass manufacturer&quot; of the level you mention won't really be perceived well by the other Garou or the spirits.<br /> <br /> A Fetish is an extraordinary act of commitment and duty for a spirit. The Garou owe them respect for that.<br /> <br /> As for maximum number, sure. It might not be spelled out, but you still need to attune to them, and I doubt the spirits would be happy to be sharing the road with another dozen stuffed in your bag. It could make any further attunement harder as well as make it harder to make new fetishes considering the bargains you need to make to even create one.<br /> <br /> This of course completely goes against the whole fact that fetishes are<b> rare</b>, and that any occasion when one is made is a deed worth celebrating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:02:32-07:00","id":1486691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486680#post1486680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ST will certainly define what is possible but still it's strange that the game talk about sacred object without talking about the possibility of characters fully stuffed with them, especially when no rule tell it's impossible. I know more than one pc that will try to play on this lack of detail</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read through the answers in this thread again. They provide many, many reasons why this is not a feasible situation in the default setting of WtA. This is not necessarily the same setting you want to play for your chronicle, but you can hardly blame the rules if you change the setting they were written for. And if you feel it needs to be addressed, you can make a house rule; in my first answer I mentioned I have one to limit the number of fetishes a character can have attuned. Use that if you feel you have to.<br /> <br /> By the way, giving the players everything they want does not mean it will result in more fun or a better story. I'm all for incorporating player ideas into the narrative, but if you think it would be disruptive, it's ok to say No sometimes. That's part of being a ST, too","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:32:39-07:00","id":1486695,"title":"","content":"Talking things out with your players is important. Some players are fine with their PCs chasing an impossible dream as long as they know that as players it's impossible. Some players are fine to hear that something is theoretically possible but will be extremely difficult and unlikely to see success in play as a &quot;soft&quot; no (what feels overpowered or excessive at the start of the game might seem more reasonable when the PCs are all high XP elders on the verge of becoming Legends). Others will readjust to something easier to accomplish in the scope of your chronicle. <br /> <br /> Let the players know where you stand: what's a hard no, what's a soft no, what's something they can try but you're not going to make easy, etc. Then hear what they have to say, while remembering that you have to have fun running the game for them to have fun playing it; and if saying no is important to you having fun, they need to respect that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:43:39-07:00","id":1486741,"title":"","content":"The idea of a legendary garou which successfully who succeeded in making a whole panoply of spirits work together in the form of fetishes by his merit and honor seems possible for me when he's rank 5 or 6. Of course i've heard you all, spirits can be not happy to be used as simple tools among many others, but as conscious and resonant beings it's possible to talk with them, biuld a temporary team, or make them work all together with a powerfull and honorable Garou<br /> <br /> Of course fetishes are rare, so that would be even rarier to meet that kind of warrior, but characters like Albercht would certainly be able to accomplish the feat of wear large variety of fetish<br /> <br /> i didn't plan to allows my pc's to do the same, 1 fetishes or 2 per characters is enough, it's the possibility of achieving it in particular circumstances or by a very great merit which is interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-17-2022, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T02:56:27-07:00","id":1486748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486741#post1486741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a legendary garou which successfully who succeeded in making a whole panoply of spirits work together in the form of fetishes by his merit and honor seems possible for me when he's rank 5 or 6. Of course i've heard you all, spirits can be not happy to be used as simple tools among many others, but as conscious and resonant beings it's possible to talk with them, biuld a temporary team, or make them work all together with a powerfull and honorable Garou<br /> <br /> Of course fetishes are rare, so that would be even rarier to meet that kind of warrior, but characters like Albercht would certainly be able to accomplish the feat of wear large variety of fetish<br /> <br /> i didn't plan to allows my pc's to do the same, 1 fetishes or 2 per characters is enough, it's the possibility of achieving it in particular circumstances or by a very great merit which is interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that your perception of scale is off. Albrecht is the King of the Garou and he has TWO fetishes to his name. His pack has two legendary members - both with zero fetishes - Mari Cabarah (a <b>Theurge)</b> and Evan heals the past. Let's go into a couple more legends wile we're there - Yuri Konietzko, another Theurge and a sneaky git at that, has ONE, Golgol Fangs First has two and Zhyzhak has ONE.<br /> <br /> Sure, all of them could get a fetish or two if circumstances and need came to them that they needed it, but they would not be making them en masse nor would they be hoarding them. They would either borrow them or claim them through cultural methods. Making a fetish is hard and it's a huge commitment of resources. A Rank 5/6 Theurge fetishmaker would not be making them for himself, he would be making them for others. Making a fetish is not one roll and one night, it's a project with preparation times lasting in weeks to months and even the best prepared master of fetishes can mess up wasting all the time and effort. So anyone who is an experienced Fetish maker spends a lot of time in preparation, collection of materials, appeasing spirits and purifying themselves. This takes time, and they have other non fetish-making duties and needs in their lives.<br /> <br /> A garou with 2 fetishes to his name is a rarity. Your hypothetical &quot;loaded&quot; Garou is not supported by the setting as presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T04:53:34-07:00","id":1486758,"title":"","content":"To be fair, rarity also depends on the level of the fetish. A character having a <i>Magpie's Swag</i> fetish could be likened to a mortal owning an expensive car- not common, a bit unusual, but not on the level of seeing someone in full Armor of the Gods dual-wielding Excaliburs. As with most scales, I tend to view the rarity increase exponentially with the level. The crafting systems (and by extension, characters who focus on fetish crafting) also work a lot better for low-level fetishes.<br /> <br /> A character rocking a dozen Level 1 fetishes would still run into the problem of having to manage a car-park of sentient cars who demand equal attention, service, don't like each other, are jealous, and at some point simply refuse to start up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T05:40:11-07:00","id":1486761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486758#post1486758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, rarity also depends on the level of the fetish. A character having a <i>Magpie's Swag</i> fetish could be likened to a mortal owning an expensive car- not common, a bit unusual, but not on the level of seeing someone in full Armor of the Gods dual-wielding Excaliburs. As with most scales, I tend to view the rarity increase exponentially with the level. The crafting systems (and by extension, characters who focus on fetish crafting) also work a lot better for low-level fetishes.<br /> <br /> A character rocking a dozen Level 1 fetishes would still run into the problem of having to manage a car-park of sentient cars who demand equal attention, service, don't like each other, are jealous, and at some point simply refuse to start up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutley agreed on importance of fetishes. But considering what level 1 fetishes tend to do, it's not what the minmaxer will gravitate to, The 3-5 has the cool stuff. And I can totally see a Theurge with a collection of spiritual tools, but I see that as maybe a total of 4-5 fetishes of rank 1-2, not a dozen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T08:27:12-07:00","id":1486770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486748#post1486748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that your perception of scale is off. Albrecht is the King of the Garou and he has TWO fetishes to his name. His pack has two legendary members - both with zero fetishes - Mari Cabarah (a <b>Theurge)</b> and Evan heals the past. Let's go into a couple more legends wile we're there - Yuri Konietzko, another Theurge and a sneaky git at that, has ONE, Golgol Fangs First has two and Zhyzhak has ONE.<br /> <br /> Sure, all of them could get a fetish or two if circumstances and need came to them that they needed it, but they would not be making them en masse nor would they be hoarding them. They would either borrow them or claim them through cultural methods. Making a fetish is hard and it's a huge commitment of resources. A Rank 5/6 Theurge fetishmaker would not be making them for himself, he would be making them for others. Making a fetish is not one roll and one night, it's a project with preparation times lasting in weeks to months and even the best prepared master of fetishes can mess up wasting all the time and effort. So anyone who is an experienced Fetish maker spends a lot of time in preparation, collection of materials, appeasing spirits and purifying themselves. This takes time, and they have other non fetish-making duties and needs in their lives.<br /> <br /> A garou with 2 fetishes to his name is a rarity. Your hypothetical &quot;loaded&quot; Garou is not supported by the setting as presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quibble - Margrave Konietzko also has a grand klaive, and Evan has a spear that can summon lightning. Still not exactly bristling with them, though, especially since Thunder's Bracers are explicitly noted as being extremely difficult to create, along with I believe a similar Shadow Lord-specific fetish from H&amp;K that requires some BSing and trickery on the part of the Lord making them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T08:44:41-07:00","id":1486772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486770#post1486770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a similar Shadow Lord-specific fetish from H&amp;K</div> </div> </div> </div>For a brief moment there I thought you said the Shadow Lords get their Fetishes from Heckler &amp; Koch.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:37:19-07:00","id":1486785,"title":"","content":"In terms of the average number of fetishes that Garou have, I once reviewed several Rage books and made a census of how many fetishes and their levels individual Garou had by their rank. Here is what I discovered in general.<br /> <br /> Rank 1 and 2 Garou typically did not have fetishes, but there were exceptions with a small number of them having fetishes of any level (although it was typically low level fetishes of rank 1 or 2).<br /> <br /> Rank 3 Garou had one or more fetishes whose total level were equal to their level. This might mean one fetish of level 3, three level one fetishes, or one level 1 and one level 2 fetish. Since this is an average only, there were still Adren who had no fetishes and other Adren who had fetishes with greater combined levels, but not more than double their rank.<br /> <br /> Rank 4 or 5 Garou typically have 1 to 4 fetishes equal to their rank. Again this is average with some Garou having less or more than this. But even on the high level, these individual high ranked Garou did not seem to carry more levels in fetish than double their rank.<br /> <br /> This seemed to be the case from book to book in addition to it being the average for all the books. So it is possible this was some kind of guideline the writers of the Rage books intended. Or it may have been unintentional.<br /> <br /> In any case, this rough guideline is what I use in creating my NPCs, or allowing/providing the PCs fetishes.<br /> <br /> If someone had more fetishes than this guideline, there began to be an increased possibility other Garou with greater &quot;claim&quot; to them would begin to take them or challenge for them. &quot;That fetish is too powerful for a low ranking Garou like yourself, it's better for the Nation that someone more capable takes care of it.&quot; &quot;You have way too many fetishes. You cannot make use of all of them. It's better to surrender some to the sept leadership so they can determine who can make the best use out of them.&quot; &quot;Young Cliath, your grandfather would have wanted you to have that klaive, but you are still too young for such a burder. I will keep it safe for you until you reach the rank of Adren and be equal to its responsibility.&quot; &quot;You are being too selfish by keeping such a powerful fetish for yourself while greater Garou have none. I will correct this problem by taking it from you in worthy challenge.&quot; And so on.<br /> <br /> Every ST will have their own sweet spot in terms of fetishes and characters. But I found this works for me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:52:58-07:00","id":1486788,"title":"","content":"Technically, there's only one Rage book (Warriors of the Apocalypse, a handy book of NPCs). Also, Garou Law or not, having a higher-ranked character commandeer a fetish paid for in chargen is more than a little bit of a dick move, and you might find players getting sparse after doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486772#post1486772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a brief moment there I thought you said the Shadow Lords get their Fetishes from Heckler &amp; Koch.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was noted as a lucky coincidence back when the book came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T13:53:11-07:00","id":1486796,"title":"","content":"I always balk a bit when it comes to using the WtA book NPCs because... they're so far divorced from what the PCs are capable of getting. This has come up multiple times in the past in regards to other topics, I'd rather not rehash it here too much, but when you look at any supernatural trait in WtA, the NPCs frequently have fairly low ratings for their stated status in the game.<br /> <br /> I don't know of many players that are really thinking about things to be easily convinced by the argument &quot;look at how few Fetishes the NPCs have,&quot; when the players are likely to have x2 to x5 as many Gifts and Rites as the NPCs do, and frequently put a lot more into Gnosis as well (Rage is at least something players can see the point of not going for as high a rating as possible until later in the game when they have more tools to offset drawbacks).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T14:53:10-07:00","id":1486799,"title":"","content":"Maybe my visions of spirits is incomplete, then...<br /> From what i understood, spirits exist in the umbra to fulfil a task. That task depend of their nature and the more important it is the more powerful the spirit get. <br /> An average wolf spirit will be a Gafflins while the alpha of a pack or a powerfull protector of it's kind will be a jagglins<br /> <br /> When talking about fetishe the garou must create a &quot;home&quot; to the spirit he has in mind, that require a very great skill and must be in accordance with that specific spirit. Once done he must find or summon the spirit and convince him being bond permanently to the object. <br /> <br /> Now, if werewolves know that the end is near, spirits are clearly among the firsts victims, the wyrm corrupting them everywhere. Of course be bond to an object prevent them to fulfil their duty but they can accept to engage in the war to save Gaia. With that in mind (again i'm surely wrong i don't have years of game behind me yet) their &quot;whims&quot; seams either immature or contemptuous. I mean, their world is going to die, their influence is fading, and if a valuable garou wear more than 3 of them at the same time they refuse to cooperate??? Really??? is it really like this the game in story and rules work?<br /> <br /> In addition the jagglins can think, talk with garou, as fetishes they're not treated as object but as ally, friends and they're thank as such when the fight is over<br /> <br /> If someone use them for insignificant purpose or without respect for them i understand they would resist, but the same way garou fights as pack and can be from different race, tribes and auspice and even with other ferae why spirits would refuse to work with their other kind ? Especially to save their own existence and their world? In peace time most of them would refuse to be bound permanently to objects and even in that case they would demand for veneration and absolute respect, but it's the apocalypse<br /> <br /> Most will prefer staying free instead of being trapped and fight on their own of course, that explain the rarity of fetishes, but those who accepted to be bound sacrifice their freedom to help garou to save them any time needed. So refuse to work with more than 2 or 3 other fetishe while they're respected, thanked and treated as brothers (because after all werewolves are half spirits, so litteraly their brothers and protector) sound wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-17-2022, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T16:11:31-07:00","id":1486803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486799#post1486799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe my visions of spirits is incomplete, then...<br /> From what i understood, spirits exist in the umbra to fulfil a task. That task depend of their nature and the more important it is the more powerful the spirit get.<br /> An average wolf spirit will be a Gafflins while the alpha of a pack or a powerfull protector of it's kind will be a jagglins</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true for wolf spirits, but on average, spirits are highly individualistic. Their behavior (and needs) resemble the qualities of whatever the spirit represents. A magpie spirit will be social, curious, and attracted to sparkly baubles. A car spirit will want to be agile, a stone spirit may have a slow and lethargic personality, and so on. A spirit that is 'compatible' with the function of a Fetish is thus easier to convince to perform its function as the Fetish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486799#post1486799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When talking about fetishe the garou must create a &quot;home&quot; to the spirit he has in mind, that require a very great skill and must be in accordance with that specific spirit. Once done he must find or summon the spirit and convince him being bond permanently to the object.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is correct. The spirit is giving up its freedom and independence and will want something in return for that- imagine you are an effectively immortal being and someone asks you to jump into a box so you can be their calculator for the rest of your existence! You will want a good bargain for that and better enjoy maths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486799#post1486799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if werewolves know that the end is near, spirits are clearly among the firsts victims, the wyrm corrupting them everywhere. Of course be bond to an object prevent them to fulfil their duty but they can accept to engage in the war to save Gaia. With that in mind (again i'm surely wrong i don't have years of game behind me yet) their &quot;whims&quot; seams either immature or contemptuous. I mean, their world is going to die, their influence is fading, and if a valuable garou wear more than 3 of them at the same time they refuse to cooperate??? Really??? is it really like this the game in story and rules work?</div> </div> </div> </div> Best think of spirits as people, because they are. They are very extraordinary people, but still have personalities. Pick three random strangers from the street and ask them to follow you around, because the world is ending and you need their help. Sure, maybe you can convince them. Maybe they will do their best to help. But that doesn't mean they get along with each other, nor does it mean they are only concerned with your task. They also have their own lives and interests.<br /> <br /> Or think of it this way: if one of your PCs had three spirits in their service who would be played by three other players, how long do you think it would take for them to have their first argument?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486799#post1486799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition the jagglins can think, talk with garou, as fetishes they're not treated as object but as ally, friends and they're thank as such when the fight is over<br /> <br /> If someone use them for insignificant purpose or without respect for them i understand they would resist, but the same way garou fights as pack and can be from different race, tribes and auspice and even with other ferae why spirits would refuse to work with their other kind ? Especially to save their own existence and their world? In peace time most of them would refuse to be bound permanently to objects and even in that case they would demand for veneration and absolute respect, but it's the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Most will prefer staying free instead of being trapped and fight on their own of course, that explain the rarity of fetishes, but those who accepted to be bound sacrifice their freedom to help garou to save them any time needed. So refuse to work with more than 2 or 3 other fetishe while they're respected, thanked and treated as brothers (because after all werewolves are half spirits, so litteraly their brothers and protector) sound wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>'The world is ending' is actually a really good argument to present, especially if the Fetish user is honoring their side of the pact. It just needs to be convincing that whatever you are doing with the Fetish <i>is </i>relevant and important to the cause. Honestly, if the Fetish user is being respectful and is not using the Fetishes in profane ways, chances of the spirits getting grumpy are low. But as mentioned above, powerful Fetishes tend to house powerful personalities. Getting many strong personalities to work together is a lot easier short term than long term.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T16:27:34-07:00","id":1486805,"title":"","content":"You are fundamentally misunderstanding spirits. They don't follow our logic, they just are, and by being they fulfil their meaning. Most of them don't care about Gaia or the war for the simple reason that it's outside their understanding of what is reality. To the lesser ones it's literally only about what they represent and what their higher ups tell them to do, and even following that is pure instinct, not reasoning or choice. To the greater ones it's about being the concept and feeding the concept to greater strength. The greatest ones can be quite prideful, haughty and feel that they are beyond mortal concerns because they are the greatest of what they represent and only seek to further that.<br /> <br /> By accepting the fate of being a fetish they stop being what they are and deny their most fundamental nature to serve in some great conflict that is very hard to comprehend for the vast majority of them. For the powerful, it's a fate worse than death, all their power, glory and respect are gone and forgotten and all their pride as the pinnacle of the concept is subsumed by a fitful sleep within a harsh brutal thing made of base material, stuck in a world that's wrong in every possible way.<br /> <br /> So yes, they are allies to the Garou in so far as there are ancient pacts, deals with certain broods and Garou offer them the right appropriation, or service that furthers their brood. but they have no reason or comprehension of how mortals actually live and what they are concerned about. That's pretty much why spirit speech isn't literal language, but interpreting the idiosyncratic nature of the ephemeral being you are communing with. The reason they help is because they are told to, or given enough respect and power (Gnosis) to sacrifice their purpose for a while. Consider it like this, forcing a spirit into a fetish is like telling a river to stop flowing. Once it does that it's no longer a river.<br /> <br /> There are spirits with agendas that extend into the real world, and that actually kinda comprehend the mortal world and it's intricacies. Those are of great power and the least likely to ever get into a fetish or a talen. The City Fathers, the Totems or the Celestials are glorious beings beyond such trivialities.<br /> <br /> The other side of the coin is that the Garou understand and respect this. They follow the ancient pacts and rules and make this service as little a burden as they can on their strange kin, because they know that if they don't the bad reputation and disrespect will breed contempt and create a rift that will never mend. Pushing these lines and creating friction between the Garou and the spirits is the best way to get your arse handed to you by the other Garou who understand how frail this system actually is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:16:08-07:00","id":1486816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486799#post1486799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe my visions of spirits is incomplete, then...<br /> From what i understood, spirits exist in the umbra to fulfil a task. That task depend of their nature and the more important it is the more powerful the spirit get.<br /> An average wolf spirit will be a Gafflins while the <b>alpha of a pack</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>[DRAMATIC EYEBROW RAISE]<br /> <br /> A <i>what</i>, now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T00:59:16-07:00","id":1486852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486805#post1486805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes, they are allies to the Garou in so far as there are ancient pacts, deals with certain broods and Garou offer them the right appropriation, or service that furthers their brood. but they have no reason or comprehension of how mortals actually live and what they are concerned about. That's pretty much why spirit speech isn't literal language, but interpreting the idiosyncratic nature of the ephemeral being you are communing with. The reason they help is because they are told to, or given enough respect and power (Gnosis) to sacrifice their purpose for a while. Consider it like this, forcing a spirit into a fetish is like telling a river to stop flowing. Once it does that it's no longer a river.<br /> <br /> There are spirits with agendas that extend into the real world, and that actually kinda comprehend the mortal world and it's intricacies. Those are of great power and the least likely to ever get into a fetish or a talen. The City Fathers, the Totems or the Celestials are glorious beings beyond such trivialities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the argument, but somehow it make me think of the ents in lord of the ring, beings which are not concerned by the war for their own reason. Until they discover that the war already took them something important and they realize that they just cannot stay out of this<br /> The prophecy of the Phoenix (at least the last sign in the comic at the beggining of the book) tell that at the end an army of all tribes with all their totem and their allies will fight the wyrm and overcome him and his forces once and for all, and when tou know what being are his most powerfull warriors (zhyzack, number 2....) their help for this ultimate battle is vital<br /> You can take in addition the exemple of griffon, he's a totem but he and his spirits tend to hate humanity because of what they did and continue to do the the living being on earth, i can't imagine griffon and his spirits refuse to help garou to fight the wyrm<br /> <br /> I already told i understand that spirit lose their freedom and part of their nature when they're bond into fetishes, but even if it's rare and difficult to accomplish the idea of a rank 5 garou gathering year after year fetishe he created himself with spirits he already know for a long time and wearing them as brothers in arms, calling for their help only if needed and to protect their world and their kind isn't something impossible to me. <br /> Unique of course maybe in all garou nation they would be only 1 or 2 warrior capable of such a feat but not impossible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-18-2022, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T17:49:18-07:00","id":1486929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1486410-multiple-fetiche?p=1486799#post1486799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if werewolves know that the end is near, spirits are clearly among the firsts victims, the wyrm corrupting them everywhere. Of course be bond to an object prevent them to fulfil their duty but they can accept to engage in the war to save Gaia. With that in mind (again i'm surely wrong i don't have years of game behind me yet) their &quot;whims&quot; seams either immature or contemptuous. I mean, their world is going to die, their influence is fading, and if a valuable garou wear more than 3 of them at the same time they refuse to cooperate??? Really??? is it really like this the game in story and rules work?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was the ST, and this was a character's appeal to the spirits, my reply would be in several ways. <br /> <br /> First, spirits have their own tasks to do that are important for the world. Especially now since there are fewer active spirits than there once were. Therefore, spirits have an opportunity cost when they enter a fetish. They aren't doing their actual purpose while they are in the fetish. Which is more important - how the fetish is going to be used, or the activities they would otherwise get to do? The idea that the ONLY or PRIMARY important thing for a spirit is to enter a fetish is ultimately wrong in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Second, if you are going to argue that the world is going to end and the spirits are not doing their jobs if they don't enter your fetish, you are setting yourself up at a very high standard. &quot;How will you having gravity boots save the world? How is you having a bladed glove save the world? How will you having a shoulder cannon save the world?&quot; &quot;You already have all these other fetishes where you promised to save the world, but haven't. Why should I trust you when you already lied to these other spirits that you were going to save the world?&quot; &quot;What is your plan for saving the world. I am very interested in how using a fetish empowered by me will do so. Please explain.&quot; My suspicion is that the character can't actually explain any of that. In truth, the character just wants to make himself more powerful and has an inflated opinion of his own importance. Yeah, he'll fight the Wyrm using those things. As will lots of other Garou who won't have those things and probably do just as good of a job as he does.<br /> <br /> Third, the entire argument smacks of ego and hubris. This Garou, who has been alive less than a century, is attempting to explain to the spirits who have witnessed all sorts of conflicts, acts of heroism, history, and so on for millennia that predate the Garou. Expect a reply on the same level of &quot;Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth? Tell me, if you know so much.&quot; It's a lot different if you are a Rank 6 Garou who has a long established history of doing actions that the spirits approve of, who needs a specific help for a specific quest that is clearly related to ending a particular threat forever, and some yahoo Garou with middling accomplishments as an Adren or lower Rank asking for generic help. The Garou do not necessarily know more or are wiser than the spirits. Their entire history proves otherwise.<br /> <br /> Fourth, the spirits could easily turn the argument around the Garou. &quot;We know better than you what to do. Therefore, you should serve us, do our bidding in all things, because we can make better use of you in fighting the Wyrm than you can on your own.&quot; How many Garou are going to accept that argument? How many PCs? Almost none, because nobody wants to be a slave. The PC is going to come up with all sorts of reasons not to do so, or ask a lot of specific of the spirit on how exactly this will help, or offer some alternative. In other words, the PC is going to reject the very basis of his own argument.<br /> <br /> Fifth, how many centuries have the Garou been making arguments like this? And there's been no final battle. Yeah, the contemporary setting implies they are living in the end times right now, but how many chronicles actually deal with the actual end of the world? I'm sure some STs have ran an actual end of the world chronicle using the material in Apocalypse or their own. But I think those are probably very rare compared to all the other chronicles that are run. And in those that were, how many actually required a Garou to have gravity boots, shoulder cannons, and bladed gloves? If that is the kind of chronicle an ST is running where some Garou with gravity boots is decisive to winning the whole thing, yeah, then as an ST I'd go with it. Great argument then. But I would be very surprised if most are that kind of chronicle.<br /> <br /> So as good as this sounds to you, to my ears it's the typical BS people use when they are being self-serving but want to disguise it. Those gravity boots are not going to be the key to preventing the Apocalypse. Showing more humility, being less greedy, appreciating the sacrifice the spirit is making, and agreeing to some kind of substantial chiminage is a much better approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are lots of fetishes out there. Somebody has to be making them. And I'm sure it's a relatively small number of Garou who have made most of the fetishes used by their septs than individual Garou making a single fetish or so during their life. I also think that 1) that is probably not the most exciting thing for a PC to do. They don't want to spend much of their time crafting. This is probably best done by NPCs who have already experienced a lot, and are now mostly retired supporting their people in other ways. and who has a proven track record to the spirits that he is someone they can trust during the negotiations for fetish creation. And 2) gradually behaving stranger and stranger because of the chiminage requirements for each of the spirits they used to make the fetish. and 3) Ultimately the total number of fetishes out there do not indicate a disrespect or greed by the Garou Nation in general towards the spirits. <br /> <br /> \u200bDifferent STs can come to different conclusions on the specifics, but any kind of mass production of fetishes seems counter to the setting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T12:52:24-07:00","id":1487046,"title":"","content":"My house rule has always been that a person can have a total number of fetishes with a combined level that is no higher than their gnosis (i.e. if a character has 3 gnosis they can have a lvl 1 and a lvl 2 fetish, or a lvl 3 fetish, or 3 level 1 fetishes), but that is secondary to the overall rarity of fetishes in the world. As a result you seldom find packs at my table with more than one or two fetishes between them at most.<br /> <br /> Talens I see as a different ball of wax. The spirits bound to those have agreed to perform a single task, whereupon they'll be released. It stands to reason they'd be more likely to agree to being bound if their release is imminent and they stand to gain something from it. To that end I allow players at my table to have the same limit on talens, but that they don't impact their fetishes.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting, even if there was such a character that had many fetishes, there's <b>no</b> way they'd have enough gnosis to activate them all. That's the main reason why I implemented the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}